course: dictionary
lesson: 13665
title: Who gives the information?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An informant is a person who gives information to someone else. The word comes from «inform», which means to tell someone something. Ask yourself: who is telling, and who is being told? In «The researcher asked her informant about the village's old songs», the informant is the person answering the researcher's questions.
explain: Context clues help you here. «The detective met a nervous informant in a dark car park.» Nervous and dark car park suggest a secret meeting, so the informant is probably giving the police secret information about a crime. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a nervous person who gives information" still makes sense.
explain: The same word can fit very different stories. A scientist, a journalist and a police officer can all have informants, but the job is always the same: the informant gives information. Some informants are happy to be named, and some want to stay hidden.
fact: An informant is a person who gives information to someone else.
fact: «Informant» can mean a person who answers questions for a researcher, for example about their language or customs.
fact: «Informant» can also mean a person who secretly gives the police information about crimes; this person is also called an informer.
fact: In detective stories, slang words for an informant include «grass» and «snitch».
fact: In news, a journalist may protect an informant's name, so that nobody else finds out who it is.
exercise: The researcher asked her informant about the village's old songs. What is an informant here? | A person who sings the songs very loudly | A book full of pictures | A village that is very old | *A person who gives information to someone else
exercise: The detective met a nervous informant in a dark car park, who whispered the name of the thief. What is the informant doing? | *Secretly giving the police information about a crime | Taking a photo of the car park | Stealing the thief's bag
exercise: The journalist promised to protect the informant. Find and copy the word that means the person who gave the information. | *informant | promised | journalist | protect
test: «The scientist thanked her informants for sharing stories about their childhood.» Here, informants are | *People who gave information by answering questions | People who wrote the book | Police officers searching for a thief
test: Which slang word for an informant is used in detective stories? | guard | teacher | singer | *snitch
exam: Which sentence uses informant correctly? | *The informant told the police where the stolen car was hidden | The informant painted the kitchen wall bright blue | The informant swam across the lake every morning | The informant was a very large and warm pizza
